  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incentive Fund Phase IV 2015-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incentive Fund is an infrastructure program that has been in operation since 2000 and aims to attract, identify and incentivise high performing organisations to expand the reach, coverage and quality of their contribution to social and economic development in Papua New Guinea. Projects previously funded include the redevelopment of markets, construction of bridges, a hydropower system, school buildings and health facilities. Phase 4 of the Incentive Fund (IF4), like its predecessors, continues to support activities in a wide range of sectors including health, education, water and sanitation, agriculture and rural development but with a new focus on innovation and private sector development. 

Sector split: Infrastructure 100%</narrative>
  </description>
